  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "processMSG",
    "file": "open62541/src/server/ua_server_binary.c",
    "description": "Heap use-after-free of the connection send buffer occurs because processMSG frees request/response members that alias memory owned by the connection input buffer, and then later error handling in processBinaryMessage calls UA_Connection_sendError, which requests a send buffer from the same network-layer buffer and writes into it. In this PoV, UA_deleteMembers in processMSG (line ~562 cleanup path) releases memory that is actually the preallocated connection buffer (allocated in createDummyConnection), leaving connection->getSendBuffer to return a dangling pointer that is written by UA_TcpMessageHeader_encodeBinary/UInt32_encodeBinary.",
    "conditions": "Via fuzz_binary_message, crafted HEL/OPN/MSG chunks drive decoding in processMSG so that decoded members point into the connection buffer and cleanup runs UA_deleteMembers on them (error path). processBinaryMessage then sees non-GOOD retval and sends ERR via UA_Connection_sendError. The test network layer reuses the freed connection buffer as send buffer, so encoding the ERR header writes to freed memory (UAF). Trigger requires malformed message causing processMSG failure after decoded dynamic fields are set and then cleanup+ERR path executes."
  },
